1
00:00:03,500 --> 00:00:07,900
So, what's the big news you had us rush all the way over here for?
是什麼天驚地動的大消息 要我們馬上趕過來？

2
00:00:08,070 --> 00:00:09,870
It took you 45 minutes to cross a street.
你們光過個馬路就花了四十五分鐘

3
00:00:10,040 --> 00:00:12,770
Come on, guys. It's just one baby.
真是的，只不過是個嬰兒

4
00:00:14,880 --> 00:00:17,670
Oh, sure, now you guys clam up.
好吧，你們現在都沒有人要幫腔

5
00:00:18,650 --> 00:00:23,210
Our news. My company has asked me to head up our office in Tulsa.
我們要宣佈的消息就是 公司要我去土爾沙帶領新的分公司

6
00:00:23,390 --> 00:00:25,820
So as of Monday, I'm being officially relocated.
所以從星期一開始 我已經正式被調職了

7
00:00:25,990 --> 00:00:27,680
- Oh, my God! - What? Monday?
-喔，我的天！ -什麼？星期一？

8
00:00:27,860 --> 00:00:31,260
- How long do you have to go for? - They said it could be up to a year.
-你得要去多久呢？ -他們說有可能會長達一年

9
00:00:31,430 --> 00:00:33,790
- A year? - Well, do you have to go?
-一年？ -那你也要去嗎？

10
00:00:36,330 --> 00:00:38,420
Well, I kind of have to, don't I?
我似乎是沒有選擇，不是嗎？

11
00:00:38,600 --> 00:00:41,540
Because of this stupid thing.
都是因為這個愚蠢的東西

12
00:00:44,570 --> 00:00:48,010
There's nothing like the support of your loving wife, huh?
再也沒有比愛妻的支持 更棒的東西了

13
00:00:48,180 --> 00:00:50,510
Wait a minute. Wait, you can't go to Tulsa.
等一下，你不能去土爾沙

14
00:00:50,680 --> 00:00:54,610
Maybe you forgot, but we have tickets to the Jets game next week!
也許你忘了 但是下星期我們要去看球賽的！

15
00:00:54,820 --> 00:00:57,550
I'm sorry, but I don't think I'll be able to make it.
我很抱歉，但是我想我可能去不了

16
00:00:58,020 --> 00:01:00,920
But we were gonna go see the Jets!
但是我們是要去看球賽耶！

17
00:01:02,890 --> 00:01:07,090
You can't go. I mean, you're the glue that holds this group together.
你不能離開我們 你就像是維繫這個圈子的靈魂人物

18
00:01:07,560 --> 00:01:10,030
- Really? - Not you.
-真的嗎？ -不是你

19
00:01:13,840 --> 00:01:15,670
This whole thing is gonna be okay.
一切都會沒問題的

20
00:01:15,840 --> 00:01:19,530
They said they'd rent us a house in the suburbs. You guys can come and visit.
他們會幫我們在郊區租房子 你們可以過來看我們

21
00:01:19,710 --> 00:01:22,270
Oh, God, that is so not gonna happen.
喔，天啊，那真的是不太可能

22
00:01:24,680 --> 00:01:26,940
I can't believe you guys are moving.
我真不敢相信你們要搬走了

23
00:01:29,680 --> 00:01:31,910
- I call their apartment! - No!
-我承接他們的公寓！ -不行！

24
00:01:34,194 --> 00:01:36,287
The One With The Pediatrician

00:01:37,194 --> 00:01:38,287
rainystar壓制iPod-MP4

25
00:02:19,900 --> 00:02:22,130
- Here you go, Rach. - Thank you, Joey.
-咖啡來了，瑞秋 -謝謝你，喬伊

26
00:02:22,300 --> 00:02:25,760
You know what? I'm not even sure I can have caffeine.
你知道嗎？ 我不確定可不可以喝有咖啡因的東西

27
00:02:25,940 --> 00:02:29,970
I went through this with Ben and Carol. One coffee won't affect your milk.
我養育班還有凱蘿的經驗告訴我 一杯咖啡不會影響你的母乳的

28
00:02:30,180 --> 00:02:34,110
Just to be sure, I'm gonna call Dr. Wiener.
為了安全起見 我要打電話給歪愣醫師

29
00:02:37,790 --> 00:02:40,190
Every time?
這麼好笑嗎？

30
00:02:40,760 --> 00:02:43,950
You don't have to call him whenever you have a question, okay?
沒有必要每次有問題 都打電話給他，好嗎？

31
00:02:44,130 --> 00:02:48,930
- Trust me. I know this. - All right. I trust you.
-相信我，我是有經驗的 -好吧，我相信你

32
00:02:49,460 --> 00:02:51,830
I can see you dialing. I don't understand why..
我看到你在撥電話 我不瞭解為什麼…

33
00:02:52,000 --> 00:02:55,560
I'm on the phone! Dr. Wiener?
我在講電話！歪愣醫師嗎？

34
00:02:56,700 --> 00:03:01,230
It's so weird seeing Ross and Rachel with a baby. It's just so grownup.
看到羅斯跟瑞秋有了小孩 真是奇怪，好像大人

35
00:03:01,410 --> 00:03:05,740
I know, yeah. I feel like we're all growing up.
我知道，是啊

36
00:03:03,917 --> 00:03:05,282
覺得好像我們都一起長大了

37
00:03:05,910 --> 00:03:08,610
A person named "Wiener." God, that kills me.
有人的名字叫「歪愣」 真是笑死我了

38
00:03:09,580 --> 00:03:13,780
- Look at you all grownup. - Well, actually, you know what?
-瞧瞧你就像個大人 -事實上，你知道嗎？

39
00:03:14,260 --> 00:03:15,750
I am, you know?
我的確是長大了，知道嗎？

40
00:03:15,920 --> 00:03:18,790
Well, that whole thing with Rachel made me realize..
跟瑞秋發生的那件事讓我意識到…

41
00:03:18,960 --> 00:03:22,620
that maybe I'm ready for a more serious relationship, you know?
或許我已經準備好 要接受更認真的交往了

43
00:03:22,800 --> 00:03:26,320
Like, I'd like to meet a nice, mature, commitment-minded lady.
我想要找一個 善良、成熟、穩重的女孩子

44
00:03:26,500 --> 00:03:29,600
And looks aren't as important as..
外表並不是非常…

46
00:03:29,970 --> 00:03:31,530
Nah, she's gotta be hot.
不，她一定要很辣才行

47
00:03:32,510 --> 00:03:34,530
You know, I might know somebody.
我也許認識這樣的人

48
00:03:34,740 --> 00:03:37,510
How about you set me up with someone, and we double-date?
要不要你幫我找個對象 然後我們一起兩對約會

49
00:03:37,680 --> 00:03:39,980
I can do that. Yeah. How's Friday?
我可以啊，星期五怎樣呢？

50
00:03:40,150 --> 00:03:41,170
- Done! - All right.
-沒問題！ -好的

51
00:03:41,350 --> 00:03:43,510
Good, really? Okay, let's see.
很好，真的？ 好，我們來看看

52
00:03:44,790 --> 00:03:46,780
All right.
好的

53
00:03:47,160 --> 00:03:49,780
You know who's great? Sandy Poopack.
你知道誰不錯嗎？珊蒂普霸

54
00:03:51,460 --> 00:03:53,260
"Poopack"?
「普霸」？

55
00:03:55,960 --> 00:04:00,260
Yeah. All right. Well, that rules out Lana Titwyler.
好吧，沒關係 那萊娜緹婉樂可能也不行了

56
00:04:04,810 --> 00:04:08,870
- I've got good news. - You got out of the whole Tulsa thing?
-我有好消息 -你不用去土爾沙了嗎？

57
00:04:09,040 --> 00:04:11,530
Okay, I have news.
好吧，我有新消息

58
00:04:11,980 --> 00:04:15,610
You don't have to move to Tulsa. You can stay here and keep your job.
你不用跟我一起搬到土爾沙 你可以待在這裡，保有工作

59
00:04:15,780 --> 00:04:17,150
That's great! How?
太好了！怎麼回事？

60
00:04:17,320 --> 00:04:20,810
My boss and I worked out a deal where I'm in Tulsa four days a week.
老闆跟我達成一個協議 我一星期在土爾沙待四天就可以了

61
00:04:20,990 --> 00:04:23,120
So the other three, I can be here with you.
所以另外三天我可以跟你在一起

62
00:04:23,630 --> 00:04:26,960
So you're gonna be gone four days a week?
所以一星期有四天你不在？

63
00:04:27,960 --> 00:04:28,990
No.
不行

64
00:04:29,160 --> 00:04:32,460
I'm sorry, are you just used to saying that?
不好意思，你是不是 太習慣說不行了呢？

65
00:04:34,900 --> 00:04:37,930
No. I can't be away from you for that long.
不是，我不能跟你分開那麼久的

66
00:04:38,440 --> 00:04:40,340
- Really? - Yeah, you're my husband.
-真的嗎？ -是啊，你是我先生

67
00:04:40,510 --> 00:04:44,810
I won't live in a different state than you for 208 days out of the year.
我不要一年兩百零八天跟你住在不同州

68
00:04:45,210 --> 00:04:50,080
That's fast math. We could use you in Tulsa.
算的真快，我們土爾沙的分公司 可以聘請你的

69
00:04:51,590 --> 00:04:56,960
Thanks for trying to figure out a way, but if you go to Tulsa, I go with you.
謝謝你試著想出更好的方式 但是如果你要去土爾沙，我會跟你去

70
00:04:57,390 --> 00:04:59,380
You said that without gagging.
你這樣說的時候竟然沒有做嘔吐狀

71
00:05:00,030 --> 00:05:02,360
I know!
真的耶！

72
00:05:04,970 --> 00:05:06,700
Well, excuse me?
你說什麼？

73
00:05:06,870 --> 00:05:10,740
Oh, yeah? Well, up yours too!
喔？那你也去吃屎吧！

74
00:05:11,640 --> 00:05:14,840
- Who the hell was that? - Dr. Wiener.
-那到底是誰啊？ -歪愣醫師

75
00:05:16,940 --> 00:05:20,380
Rach, you can't call people at 3:00 in the morning.
瑞秋，你不能在凌晨三點 打電話給人家的

76
00:05:20,550 --> 00:05:23,780
You know what? You sound just like his wife.
你知道嗎？ 你聽起來就像他老婆一樣

77
00:05:24,220 --> 00:05:26,280
Was there anything even wrong with Emma?
艾□有怎樣嗎？

78
00:05:26,450 --> 00:05:30,550
Yes, of course there is! Okay? I'm not insane.
當然是有怎樣！ 好嗎？我又不是瘋了

79
00:05:31,130 --> 00:05:32,290
What was it?
是怎樣？

80
00:05:33,060 --> 00:05:35,120
Hiccups.
打嗝

81
00:05:35,300 --> 00:05:39,490
I told you, you can't call him every time any little thing comes up.
我告訴過你了，不能每次 有雞毛蒜皮小事都打電話給他

82
00:05:39,770 --> 00:05:43,760
Well, not anymore I can't. He fired us!
看來我是真的不能了 他不接我們了！

83
00:05:44,570 --> 00:05:45,970
Can you believe that?
你敢相信嗎？

84
00:05:46,140 --> 00:05:50,300
I could believe it if he came here and hit you over the head with a copy of Highlights.
我敢相信如果他在這裡 一定會用雜誌砸你的頭

85
00:05:50,480 --> 00:05:53,570
What are we gonna do? We have to find a pediatrician.
我們該怎麼辦呢？ 我們得再另找一個小兒科醫師了

86
00:05:53,750 --> 00:05:56,380
Wait, Monica said that when you guys were growing up..
等一下，摩妮卡說你們小時候…

87
00:05:56,550 --> 00:05:58,820
you liked your doctor. What was his name?
很喜歡你們的醫師 他叫什麼名字呢？

88
00:05:59,150 --> 00:06:01,140
Dr. Gettleman?
葛曼醫師嗎？

89
00:06:01,390 --> 00:06:04,050
Yeah, no, I don't think that's a good idea.
不，我認為這不是個好主意

90
00:06:04,230 --> 00:06:06,560
In fact, I think he's dead.
事實上，我想他死了

91
00:06:06,730 --> 00:06:08,790
Why does everything happen to me?
為什麼壞事都發生在我身上？

92
00:06:10,160 --> 00:06:13,290
I promise, first thing tomorrow, we'll find another doctor.
我保證，明天第一件事 就是找到一個新的醫生

93
00:06:13,470 --> 00:06:15,990
But I gotta get up early, and I'm not feeling well.
但是我要很早起床 而且我現在覺得不是很舒服

94
00:06:16,170 --> 00:06:19,110
You're not feeling well? What do you have? Rubella?
你不舒服？ 是怎麼回事呢？德國麻疹嗎？

95
00:06:19,270 --> 00:06:22,440
Because don't go near Emma, she has not had that shot.
別靠近艾□ 她還沒有注射預防針

96
00:06:22,740 --> 00:06:26,580
You know, come to think of it, it does feel rubella-like.
我仔細想想 倒還感覺像是德國麻疹

97
00:06:36,560 --> 00:06:39,290
Wiener!
歪愣！

98
00:06:39,460 --> 00:06:41,490
Wiener! Wiener! Wiener!
歪愣！歪愣！歪愣！

99
00:06:41,660 --> 00:06:42,720
Rachel!
瑞秋！

100
00:06:43,300 --> 00:06:46,100
Great! Now he's gonna know it was me!
太棒了，現在他就知道那是我了！

101
00:06:51,510 --> 00:06:53,800
And the kung pao chicken.
還有宮保雞丁

102
00:06:53,980 --> 00:06:56,140
Utensils and plates for one.
一人用的餐具

103
00:06:56,310 --> 00:06:58,800
And can you read the order back to me?
可以重複我的訂單嗎？

104
00:07:09,290 --> 00:07:10,850
Great.
太棒了

105
00:07:11,390 --> 00:07:13,830
Yeah. Okay, thanks. Bye.
好的，謝謝，再見

106
00:07:16,700 --> 00:07:20,960
So how is this for our big double date tonight?
看我為今晚我們兩對約會打扮如何？

107
00:07:21,700 --> 00:07:23,530
Oh, my God.
喔，天啊

108
00:07:24,870 --> 00:07:28,240
Great. Just the reaction I was hoping for.
太棒了，這正是我要的反應

109
00:07:28,410 --> 00:07:32,070
Yeah, so you found someone for me? You didn't forget?
是啊，你有幫我找到人嗎？ 你沒有忘記吧？

110
00:07:32,250 --> 00:07:34,710
Of course not. And you'll love Mary Ellen.
當然沒有 你會愛死□莉艾倫的

111
00:07:34,880 --> 00:07:38,440
She's really smart and cute and funny and..
她真的很聰明、可愛風趣，而且…

112
00:07:38,620 --> 00:07:43,960
I can't tell you how I know this, but she is not opposed to threesomes.
我不能告訴你我是怎麼知道的 但是她並不反對三人行

113
00:07:45,090 --> 00:07:46,220
All right.
好耶

114
00:07:46,730 --> 00:07:51,060
- So tell me something about my guy. - No.
-說一點我的約會對象吧 -不行

115
00:07:52,500 --> 00:07:55,590
Come on, give me something. What's his name?
別這樣，透露一點嘛 他叫什麼名字？

116
00:07:56,040 --> 00:07:58,900
I'm not sure I understand the question.
我不明白你的問題

117
00:08:02,080 --> 00:08:04,540
What do they call him?
大家都是怎麼叫他的？

118
00:08:05,410 --> 00:08:08,470
- Mike. - Mike. Okay, what's his last name?
-麥克 -麥克，好的，他姓什麼呢？

119
00:08:08,650 --> 00:08:12,950
Damn it! Is there no mystery left in romance anymore?!
可惡！就不能為浪漫 而保有神秘感嗎？

120
00:08:13,120 --> 00:08:16,320
We'll see you and Mike at the restaurant in a couple hours.
幾個小時之後在餐廳 與你跟麥克見

121
00:08:16,490 --> 00:08:20,450
All right, great. See you. Bye-bye.
好的，沒問題 待會見，拜拜

122
00:08:20,630 --> 00:08:25,330
Why'd I have to say Mike? I don't know a Mike! Why couldn't I have said..?
我為什麼要說麥克呢？根本不認識 誰叫麥克的！為什麼不說…？

123
00:08:27,240 --> 00:08:30,330
There's no guys in there!
這裡面根本就沒有男生！

124
00:08:33,440 --> 00:08:36,100
So this is being a parent, huh?
所以這就是帶孩子，是吧？

125
00:08:36,480 --> 00:08:39,500
I think I can handle this.
我想我可以處理得很好的

126
00:08:39,680 --> 00:08:41,670
Too intense. Too intense.
太難了，太難了

127
00:08:45,950 --> 00:08:47,110
Well, I did it.
好了，我說了

128
00:08:47,290 --> 00:08:50,050
I told my crew at the restaurant I'm heading off to Tulsa.
我告訴餐廳的班底 我要搬到土爾沙了

129
00:08:50,220 --> 00:08:53,850
- Oh, yeah? How'd they take it. - Pretty well. Yeah.
-是嗎？他們反應如何？ -還不錯

130
00:08:54,030 --> 00:08:56,460
They were brave little soldiers.
他們是勇敢的小尖兵

131
00:08:57,700 --> 00:08:59,670
Did their best to be stoic.
盡全力冷靜

132
00:08:59,830 --> 00:09:02,800
Some of them even high-fived each other to mask their pain.
有些還互相擊掌來掩飾離別的傷痛

133
00:09:05,370 --> 00:09:09,570
It's impossible to find a good doctor. How do you know the good ones..
要找好醫生真是好難 要如何分辨哪個是好醫生…

134
00:09:09,740 --> 00:09:13,340
from the ones who'll push their penis against your knee?
哪個又會拿小弟弟 摩擦你的膝蓋呢？

135
00:09:14,750 --> 00:09:15,810
Excuse me?
什麼？

136
00:09:15,980 --> 00:09:18,210
I know what she's talking about.
我知道她的意思

137
00:09:20,250 --> 00:09:24,420
You probably also had the piano teacher with the wandering hands.
你們或許也碰過 會毛手毛腳的鋼琴老師吧

138
00:09:29,160 --> 00:09:31,560
Well, we've gotta find a new pediatrician.
我們要找新的小兒科醫生

139
00:09:31,730 --> 00:09:34,760
Ross was getting sick last night, and Emma may have caught it.
羅斯昨晚不舒服 艾□或許也被感染到了

140
00:09:34,970 --> 00:09:37,870
- Why don't you see Dr. Gettleman? - Ross said he died.
-你為什麼不去找葛曼醫生呢？ -羅斯說他死了

141
00:09:38,040 --> 00:09:41,100
He didn't die. I just saw his daughter last week.
他沒死 我上星期才遇到他女兒

142
00:09:41,280 --> 00:09:46,710
She said he was fine. Her, on the other hand, botched Botox.
她說他很好，但是她呢 可被肉毒桿菌搞慘了

143
00:09:46,980 --> 00:09:49,580
Great. Well then, I'm gonna take Emma to see him.
太好了，那我要帶艾□去找他

144
00:09:49,750 --> 00:09:51,550
I wonder why Ross said that he died?
為什麼羅斯說他死了呢？

145
00:09:51,720 --> 00:09:54,590
Maybe he confused him with his childhood therapist.
或許他把他跟 他小時候的心理醫生搞混了

146
00:09:54,760 --> 00:09:55,880
He saw a therapist?
他有心理醫生？

147
00:09:56,060 --> 00:09:59,030
He used to have a recurring nightmare. It freaked him out.
他以前常常做重複的噩夢 嚇死他了

148
00:09:59,190 --> 00:10:01,250
Wow, what was it?
哇，什麼噩夢呢？

149
00:10:01,430 --> 00:10:03,120
That I was going to eat him.
夢到我要吃掉他

150
00:10:17,450 --> 00:10:19,440
Mike!
麥克！

151
00:10:20,750 --> 00:10:22,510
Yeah?
怎樣？

152
00:10:25,290 --> 00:10:27,280
Okay.
好了

153
00:10:31,230 --> 00:10:33,490
I can't believe I'm doing this with you.
真不敢相信，我竟然跟你做這件事

154
00:10:33,660 --> 00:10:36,130
Although I did just end a nine-year relationship..
我才剛結束一段九年的戀情…

155
00:10:36,300 --> 00:10:38,560
so I should be open to taking some risks.
所以我應該敞開心胸迎接一些挑戰

156
00:10:38,730 --> 00:10:41,860
That's good. Get all that boring stuff out now.
這樣很好 把那些無聊的舊東西拋掉

157
00:10:42,400 --> 00:10:45,130
Everything is gonna be fine. Follow my lead, okay?
一切安啦 跟著我就沒事，好嗎？

158
00:10:45,310 --> 00:10:47,300
All you have to do is pretend to be Mike.
你只要假裝是麥克就可以了

159
00:10:47,480 --> 00:10:49,470
- I am Mike. - Attaboy.
-我就是麥克啊 -演的真不錯

160
00:10:52,610 --> 00:10:54,100
Here they come.
她們來了

161
00:10:54,320 --> 00:10:56,480
- I'm Phoebe. - Phoebe. Mike. How you doing?
-我是菲比 -菲比，這位是麥克，你好嗎？

162
00:10:56,650 --> 00:10:59,640
- Nice to meet you. - Joey, this is Mary Ellen Jenkins.
-很高興認識你 -喬伊，這位是□莉艾倫珍金

163
00:10:59,820 --> 00:11:03,280
So, Mike, how do you and Joey know each other, anyway?
麥克，你跟喬伊是怎麼認識的呢？

164
00:11:06,530 --> 00:11:08,960
How do Joey and I know each other?
我跟喬伊是怎麼認識的呢？

165
00:11:09,130 --> 00:11:13,260
If I had a nickel for every time somebody's asked me that.
如果每次有人問我這問題 我就有五塊錢賺，那我就變富翁了

166
00:11:14,000 --> 00:11:16,400
- From school. - We met in college.
-在學校認識的 -我們在大學認識的

167
00:11:19,110 --> 00:11:21,600
I mean high school.
我是說高中

168
00:11:22,840 --> 00:11:27,140
You guys go way back, then. So, what are you up to these days?
那你們認識可久了 那你現在是做什麼的呢？

169
00:11:27,310 --> 00:11:31,510
- Well, I'm a lawyer. - Mike, attorney at law!
-我是律師 -麥克，律師！

170
00:11:31,820 --> 00:11:34,310
- Actually, I just gave up my practice. - What?
-事實上，我才剛放棄執業 -什麼？

171
00:11:34,490 --> 00:11:38,480
That's the kind of thing you usually run by me.
這種事你應該先跟我討論的

172
00:11:38,990 --> 00:11:43,330
I want to play piano professionally. If I don't do this now, I never will.
我想要成為專業鋼琴音樂家 如果現在不趕快做，就來不及了

173
00:11:43,500 --> 00:11:45,900
Great. I like that better than the lawyer thing.
太好了，我喜歡音樂家勝過律師

174
00:11:46,070 --> 00:11:50,000
Which is why I waited until now to introduce you to Mike.
這就是為什麼我等到現在 才介紹麥克給你

175
00:11:50,170 --> 00:11:52,160
You thought he was still a lawyer.
你不是還以為他是律師嗎？

176
00:11:52,340 --> 00:11:55,540
No, that's not what I meant. Let's get you a cocktail.
不，我並沒有那樣說 我們幫你點杯雞尾酒吧

177
00:12:00,150 --> 00:12:01,310
What are you doing?
你在做什麼呢？

178
00:12:01,480 --> 00:12:04,140
Looking for restaurant jobs for you in Tulsa.
幫你在土爾沙找餐廳的工作

179
00:12:04,320 --> 00:12:06,380
That's so sweet. Did you find anything?
真是窩心，有找到嗎？

180
00:12:06,550 --> 00:12:09,250
- Slim Pickins. - Nothing, huh?
-速食外餐 -什麼都沒有，是吧？

181
00:12:09,460 --> 00:12:13,420
No. Slim Pickins. It's a barbecue joint.
不，速食外餐，是間烤肉店

182
00:12:13,590 --> 00:12:17,260
They're looking for a cook. Actually, "cook" may be a bit of a stretch.
他們在找廚師，事實上 並不全然是「廚師」

183
00:12:17,470 --> 00:12:19,990
They're looking for somebody to shovel mesquite.
他們在找炒豆子的幫手

184
00:12:21,470 --> 00:12:23,870
"Slim Pickins"? That is so cheesy.
「速食外餐」？聽起來真是不高級

185
00:12:24,040 --> 00:12:26,870
Well, So Cheesy also has an opening.
「布高吉」也有在徵人

186
00:12:27,070 --> 00:12:29,870
Honey, that's okay. I know this woman, Nancy..
親愛的，沒關係 我認識一個叫南西的人…

187
00:12:30,040 --> 00:12:33,040
who's a restaurant biz headhunter. She may know something.
她是專門幫餐廳獵人頭的 她或許會知道一些職缺

188
00:12:33,210 --> 00:12:35,880
Can I say how much I appreciate you coming with me?
我真的是太感激你願意跟我去

189
00:12:36,050 --> 00:12:40,990
When we get to Tulsa, I am taking you for a great dinner at Slim Pickins.
當我們抵達土爾沙 我會帶你去速食外餐吃大餐的

190
00:12:41,560 --> 00:12:42,580
So Cheesy?
那布高吉呢？

191
00:12:44,490 --> 00:12:46,790
Whole Hog?
全豬餐廳呢？

192
00:12:47,600 --> 00:12:51,360
It's gonna be tough to keep kosher in Tulsa.
在土爾沙要找到正式餐廳還真是不簡單

193
00:12:55,440 --> 00:12:58,300
Hi, Nancy? Hi, it's Monica Geller.
嗨，南西嗎？ 嗨，我是摩妮卡蓋勒

194
00:12:58,510 --> 00:13:04,000
I'm good. Listen, I'm looking for a job in Tulsa.
我很好，我需要在土爾沙找份工作

195
00:13:04,380 --> 00:13:07,910
Yeah, well, my husband's been relocated.
是啊，因為我先生被調職到那邊

196
00:13:08,080 --> 00:13:10,610
Because I love him.
因為我愛他

197
00:13:11,050 --> 00:13:13,450
No, I don't want a job in New York.
不，我不想要紐約的工作

198
00:13:13,620 --> 00:13:16,820
Javu's looking? Oh, my God!
傑屋在找人？喔，我的天啊！

199
00:13:17,020 --> 00:13:20,980
He asked for me personally? Oh, my God!
他特別指名要我？ 喔，我的天啊！

200
00:13:21,160 --> 00:13:24,620
Wow, this is really, really flattering.
哇，我真的是太受寵若驚了

201
00:13:24,800 --> 00:13:27,630
But I'm moving to Tulsa.
但是我要搬到土爾沙了

202
00:13:27,800 --> 00:13:30,430
So, just, if you would tell Javu..
所以，請你告訴傑屋…

203
00:13:30,600 --> 00:13:32,970
I'll take it!
我接受這份工作！

204
00:13:34,040 --> 00:13:37,340
My name's Rachel Greene. I have an appointment for Emma.
我是瑞秋葛林 我有幫艾□預約看診

205
00:13:37,550 --> 00:13:41,480
Dr. Gettleman is finishing up with a patient. He'll be out shortly.
葛曼醫生快看完病人了 他等一下就會出來

206
00:13:41,650 --> 00:13:45,280
I think you just have a cold. It's definitely not strep.
我想你只是感冒了 沒有什麼嚴重性

207
00:13:45,450 --> 00:13:46,780
Thanks, doctor.
謝了，醫生

208
00:13:49,620 --> 00:13:53,860
- Would you like a lollipop? - Do you even have to ask?
-要不要來根棒棒糖呢？ -還用問嗎？

209
00:13:58,830 --> 00:14:00,960
He is alive!
他還活著！

210
00:14:05,310 --> 00:14:09,110
It's so surprising that you and Joey have known each other for so long..
好奇怪，你跟喬伊認識這麼久了…

211
00:14:09,280 --> 00:14:10,940
and I've never heard about you.
而我卻從沒有聽說過你

212
00:14:11,110 --> 00:14:15,480
That's because we had a bit of a falling out.
因為我們有吵過架

213
00:14:15,650 --> 00:14:18,640
Mike hit my mom with a car.
麥克開車撞到我媽

214
00:14:21,120 --> 00:14:25,080
- No, I didn't. - That's okay. I have forgiven you.
-才沒，我沒有 -沒關係，我已經原諒你了

215
00:14:25,260 --> 00:14:27,520
Now we're friends again, and everything's great.
現在我們又是朋友了 一切都很美好

216
00:14:27,730 --> 00:14:29,460
Well, wait. Is your mom okay?
等一下，你媽還好吧？

217
00:14:29,630 --> 00:14:33,500
Please, we're trying to have a conversation.
拜託，我們在講話耶

218
00:14:34,670 --> 00:14:36,860
You're a lot nicer on Days of Our Lives.
你在《我們的日子》中親切多了

219
00:14:37,040 --> 00:14:39,630
Days of Our Lives! That's why you look so familiar!
《我們的日子》！ 怪不得你看起來有點眼熟！

220
00:14:39,810 --> 00:14:40,900
- What? - What?
-什麼？ -什麼？

221
00:14:41,080 --> 00:14:43,200
What?
什麼？

222
00:14:43,780 --> 00:14:46,510
Do you not know each other?
你們彼此不認識嗎？

223
00:14:47,850 --> 00:14:53,310
Of course we do. He's playing a game we used to play in high school.
我們當然認識 他是在玩我們高中常玩的遊戲

224
00:14:53,490 --> 00:14:56,820
We pretend we don't know each other. We played all kinds of games.
我們假裝不認識 我們玩很多種遊戲的

225
00:14:56,990 --> 00:15:01,430
You remember that one where I punch you in the face for not being cool?
你還記得有一次 你因為太蠢而被我揍嗎？

226
00:15:03,030 --> 00:15:06,800
Let me ask you something: How many sisters does Joey have?
讓我問你一個問題 喬伊有幾個姐妹呢？

227
00:15:06,970 --> 00:15:09,870
- Six. - No, he doesn't. He has seven.
-六個 -不，他有七個

228
00:15:10,040 --> 00:15:12,510
What are you doing? I said seven!
你在搞什麼鬼？我比了七個！

229
00:15:15,810 --> 00:15:19,070
Joey, why did you set me up with a stranger?
喬伊，為什麼你要介紹陌生人給我呢？

230
00:15:19,250 --> 00:15:23,240
Because I forgot about our date. I'm so sorry.
因為我忘記了，我很抱歉

231
00:15:23,420 --> 00:15:27,820
I'm sorry too. And just to be clear, I didn't hit his mother with a car.
我也很抱歉，還有要澄清一下 我沒有開車撞他媽

232
00:15:28,160 --> 00:15:30,180
Although I'd like to be hit by one right now.
不過我現在真的很想被車撞一下

233
00:15:30,360 --> 00:15:31,720
Yeah, no problem.
是喔，沒問題

234
00:15:33,390 --> 00:15:38,090
You are unbelievable. I spent so much time finding the perfect girl for you.
你真是太不應該了 我花這麼多時間幫你找完美的對象

235
00:15:38,300 --> 00:15:41,290
Mary Ellen is really smart and cute and loose.
□莉艾倫真的很聰明 很可愛又很隨便

236
00:15:41,573 --> 00:15:43,063
嘿！

237
00:15:43,540 --> 00:15:46,170
Who are you kidding?
你別裝了吧？

238
00:15:50,440 --> 00:15:53,500
You find some guy off the street for me?
你在街上隨便捉個男的塞給我？

239
00:15:53,680 --> 00:15:55,740
God, this is humiliating!
天啊，這真是太羞辱人了！

240
00:15:55,920 --> 00:16:00,010
I'm so sorry. If you don't like this guy, I can find you a better one.
我很抱歉，如果你不喜歡這一個 我可以幫你找更好的

241
00:16:00,190 --> 00:16:02,950
Mike? Mike?
麥克？麥克？

242
00:16:03,960 --> 00:16:05,150
I'm out of here.
我要走了

243
00:16:05,630 --> 00:16:07,490
It was nice meeting you.
很高興認識你

244
00:16:07,660 --> 00:16:10,990
- You're leaving too? - I'll stay if you can tell me my name.
-你也要走？ -你說的出我的名字，我就留下

245
00:16:11,170 --> 00:16:12,390
Have a good night.
再見

246
00:16:16,640 --> 00:16:19,470
We leave tomorrow, and you still have a lot to pack.
我們明天就要走了 而你還有好多東西要打包

247
00:16:19,640 --> 00:16:20,800
You're right.
你說得對

248
00:16:21,710 --> 00:16:23,470
Maybe I shouldn't go.
或許我不應該去

249
00:16:24,650 --> 00:16:26,640
What?
什麼？

250
00:16:27,050 --> 00:16:31,510
So Nancy told me about this job at this great restaurant, Javu?
南西告訴我有一個 很棒的餐廳在徵人，傑屋？

251
00:16:31,690 --> 00:16:33,950
But it's just a little outside of Tulsa.
離土爾沙不會太遠

252
00:16:34,120 --> 00:16:35,450
Well, how far outside?
那是多遠呢？

253
00:16:36,320 --> 00:16:37,810
Manhattan?
曼哈頓遠嗎？

254
00:16:39,960 --> 00:16:43,020
And you're thinking of taking it?
你要接受這份工作嗎？

255
00:16:44,800 --> 00:16:48,360
Before, you said that being with me was more important than any job.
你之前說跟我在一起 比任何工作都重要

256
00:16:48,540 --> 00:16:53,470
But I guess now it's old job, me, new job.
但我猜，現在是 舊工作，我，新工作

257
00:16:54,810 --> 00:16:56,970
I'm gonna miss this hand!
我會想念這隻手的！

258
00:16:59,010 --> 00:17:00,710
I know this is a lot to ask..
我知道這很過份…

259
00:17:00,880 --> 00:17:03,910
but, my God, this is a once-in-a-lifetime opportunity.
但是，天啊，這是千載難逢的好機會

260
00:17:04,080 --> 00:17:07,080
What happened to "you can't live without me four days a week"?
那你說無法忍受每星期四天 要分開，是怎麼回事呢？

261
00:17:07,250 --> 00:17:12,350
Well, if you really think about it, I mean, four days is not that long.
如果你仔細想想 四天並不是很長的時間

262
00:17:12,530 --> 00:17:14,390
I see you Monday before you go to work..
星期一你去上班前我會見到你…

263
00:17:14,560 --> 00:17:16,260
and Thursday when you get back..
然後星期四晚上我也會見到你…

264
00:17:16,460 --> 00:17:20,190
and I always work late on Tuesdays, so really if you think about it..
而我總是在星期二忙得很晚 所以如果你仔細想想…

265
00:17:20,370 --> 00:17:21,770
it's really just one day.
事實上只有分開一天而已

266
00:17:21,970 --> 00:17:26,960
And well, if we can't make it one day, we got real problems, my friend.
而如果我們連一天都撐不住 我們真的是有大問題了

267
00:17:31,080 --> 00:17:34,240
- I think you should take the job. - Really?
-我認為你應該接受這份工作 -真的嗎？

268
00:17:34,420 --> 00:17:38,510
I know it must be important to you when you start chattering like a monkey.
當你開始像猴子一樣鬼吼時 我就知道這對你一定很重要

269
00:17:40,750 --> 00:17:43,590
That's the nicest thing anybody's ever said to me.
這是我聽過最美好的形容了

270
00:17:43,760 --> 00:17:45,990
It's your dream job. I can't make you pass it up.
這是你的夢想工作 我不能要求你放棄的

271
00:17:46,160 --> 00:17:47,920
Besides, I'm proud of you.
況且我還以你為榮

272
00:17:48,100 --> 00:17:49,620
- You are? - Yeah.
-真的嗎？ -是啊

273
00:17:49,800 --> 00:17:52,700
And when I get to Tulsa and people say, "Where's the missus"..
當我去到土爾沙，有人問我 「你老婆呢？」

274
00:17:52,870 --> 00:17:55,160
I'll tell them she's a chef at Javu.
我會告訴他們，她在傑屋當主廚

275
00:17:55,940 --> 00:17:58,700
And then, when they stare at me blankly..
然後，當他們 搞不清狀況盯著我看時…

276
00:17:58,870 --> 00:18:03,100
I'll make some offensive Tulsa joke, and thus, begin my isolation.
我就會說一些污辱土爾沙的笑話 然後開始被他們排擠

277
00:18:07,820 --> 00:18:10,840
- How was the pediatrician? - I really liked him.
-新醫生怎樣呢？ -我真的很喜歡他

278
00:18:11,020 --> 00:18:15,680
Yeah, yeah. It was really, really, really good.
是啊，是啊 真的，真的，真的很不錯

279
00:18:15,990 --> 00:18:19,480
- You promised not to say anything. - I know.
-你答應我不會說出去的 -我知道

280
00:18:19,660 --> 00:18:22,890
Ross still sees his pediatrician!
羅斯還在看他小時候的醫生！

281
00:18:24,500 --> 00:18:26,690
I don't care.
我不在乎

282
00:18:27,600 --> 00:18:30,870
Are you serious? You still see Dr. Gettleman?
真的嗎？ 你還在看葛曼醫師？

283
00:18:31,040 --> 00:18:33,010
He is a brilliant diagnostician!
他是醫術高明的診斷師！

284
00:18:33,170 --> 00:18:36,900
Diagnostician or boo-boo fixer?
診斷師還是醫生叔叔呢？

285
00:18:37,580 --> 00:18:40,100
Seriously, you gotta go to an appropriate doctor.
真的，你應該去看適合你的醫生才對

286
00:18:40,280 --> 00:18:43,150
And not an orthodontist..
不是牙科醫生…

287
00:18:43,320 --> 00:18:46,380
not a gynecologist..
不是婦科醫生…

288
00:18:46,550 --> 00:18:49,420
and not a veterinarian..
也更不是獸醫

289
00:18:49,620 --> 00:18:53,790
Why? I know it's a little weird, but he is a great doctor, okay?
為什麼？我知道這是有點怪 但是他是個很棒的醫生，好嗎？

290
00:18:53,960 --> 00:18:55,690
He knows my medical history.
他知道我的病史

291
00:18:55,900 --> 00:18:58,760
And every time I go in there, he makes a big deal.
而且每次我去看病 他都非常的慎重其事

292
00:18:58,930 --> 00:19:01,460
You know, "Look, it's my favorite patient."
你知道的 「瞧，這是我最喜歡的病人」

293
00:19:01,640 --> 00:19:05,300
Does he say that before he sticks his thermometer in your tushy?
是不是在把體溫計 插到你嘴裡之前說的呢？

294
00:19:05,470 --> 00:19:10,140
I seem to remember someone bringing his security blanket to college.
我還記得有人把他的 安全毛毯帶到大學宿舍

295
00:19:10,310 --> 00:19:13,210
That was not a security blanket. That was a wall hanging.
那不是安全毛毯 那是壁毯

296
00:19:13,410 --> 00:19:15,470
It didn't spend much time on the wall!
它倒是沒有被掛在牆上太久！

297
00:19:25,630 --> 00:19:27,490
Excuse me.
對不起

298
00:19:28,230 --> 00:19:31,690
Hi. I was hoping to run into you. Can we talk?
嗨，我原本就希望可以再遇到你 我們可以談談嗎？

299
00:19:32,100 --> 00:19:33,290
Sure.
當然

300
00:19:33,930 --> 00:19:36,100
Yeah. There's someone I want you to meet.
我想要介紹你認識一個人

301
00:19:36,270 --> 00:19:39,430
This is my best friend from high school.
這位是我高中最要好的朋友

302
00:19:41,180 --> 00:19:43,270
I'm sorry, I don't think I know you.
很抱歉，我並不認識你

303
00:19:43,440 --> 00:19:45,070
How hard was that?
真是太容易了

304
00:19:46,050 --> 00:19:49,710
Look, I'm sorry, really. I'm so embarrassed.
我真的很抱歉 我實在太不好意思了

305
00:19:51,520 --> 00:19:53,080
Please.
拜託

306
00:19:53,320 --> 00:19:58,350
Really, I'm a pretty nice guy. Just ask my parole officer.
真的，我是個還不錯的人 你可以問我的保釋官

307
00:20:01,300 --> 00:20:04,730
Apparently, I'm not a funny guy.
很明顯地，我並不是很風趣

308
00:20:06,170 --> 00:20:09,470
Well, why did you go along with that?
那你為什麼要這樣做呢？

309
00:20:09,640 --> 00:20:14,870
Because I was told that I'd get a free dinner, which I didn't.
因為他說，我可以吃一頓 免費的晚餐，不過並沒有

310
00:20:15,040 --> 00:20:18,270
And that I'd meet a pretty girl, which I did.
還有他說，我可以認識 漂亮的女生，這倒是有

311
00:20:20,650 --> 00:20:22,770
That's true.
那倒是真的

312
00:20:25,890 --> 00:20:28,480
Well, is anything you told me about yourself true?
那你告訴我的事有哪些是真的呢？

313
00:20:28,660 --> 00:20:31,650
My name is Mike. And I do play piano.
我的名字真的是麥克 還有我真的會彈鋼琴

314
00:20:31,830 --> 00:20:35,590
- Prove it. - There isn't a piano here.
-證明給我看 -這裡並沒有鋼琴

315
00:20:35,800 --> 00:20:39,360
That wouldn't stand in the way of a true pianist.
那對真正的鋼琴家不會是問題吧

316
00:20:40,100 --> 00:20:41,500
Okay.
好吧

317
00:20:57,950 --> 00:20:59,540
You are really good.
你真的很棒

318
00:21:03,960 --> 00:21:07,390
- I play a little guitar myself. - Really? That's great.
-我會彈一點吉他 -真的？太棒了

319
00:21:07,560 --> 00:21:11,220
- What kind of music do you play? - Like acoustic, folksy stuff, you know?
-你彈奏什麼種音樂呢？ -像是重原音、有民俗風味的

320
00:21:11,400 --> 00:21:16,270
But right now I'm working on a couple lron Maiden covers.
但是我現在在製作CD封面

321
00:21:17,840 --> 00:21:23,470
Do you think that, maybe, sometime, I could..
你想，或許，有空的話，我可…

322
00:21:23,640 --> 00:21:26,080
It's okay. Go ahead, ask me out.
沒關係的，來吧，約我吧

323
00:21:27,480 --> 00:21:31,210
Okay. You think, maybe, sometime I could take you out?
好吧，你想，或許有空的話 我可以約你出去嗎？

324
00:21:31,890 --> 00:21:34,080
You just caught me off guard.
你真是讓我一點心理準備都沒有

325
00:21:35,220 --> 00:21:37,020
Yeah, that would be nice.
好啊，我很樂意

326
00:21:37,220 --> 00:21:39,850
Look at this! My two best friends!
瞧瞧！我兩個最要好的朋友！

327
00:21:47,400 --> 00:21:50,200
Excuse me. I don't mean to be a jerk..
不好意思，我不想要太機車…

328
00:21:50,370 --> 00:21:53,900
but the baby with the rash came in after me.
但是那個長疹子的嬰兒 是在我後面進來的

329
00:21:54,740 --> 00:21:57,540
- The doctor will be right with you, sir. - I hear you..
-醫生等一下就可以看你了，先生 -我知道…

330
00:21:57,710 --> 00:21:59,840
but do you have any harder puzzles?
但是你有沒有比較高難度的謎題呢？

331
00:22:05,720 --> 00:22:07,780
Mommy, I can't find Waldo.
媽咪，我找不到華多

332
00:22:07,950 --> 00:22:09,480
What page are you on?
你在第幾頁呢？

333
00:22:09,660 --> 00:22:12,090
What, the circus? He's behind the elephant.
遊樂場嗎？他在大象後面

334
00:22:12,260 --> 00:22:15,990
Wow. So your child's a big fan of the Waldo books too?
哇，你的孩子一定也很迷華多

335
00:22:18,370 --> 00:22:21,390
Yeah, that's how I know.
是啊，所以我也很熟

336
00:22:22,100 --> 00:22:25,090
- I'm Ross, by the way. - Hi, I'm Sally.
-對了，我叫羅斯 -嗨，我叫莎莉

337
00:22:25,270 --> 00:22:29,070
So no ring. Can I assume you're also a single parent?
沒有戒指，所以我推想你也是單親？

338
00:22:29,240 --> 00:22:33,010
- I am a single parent. - It's hard, isn't it?
-我是單親沒錯 -很難，對吧？

339
00:22:33,180 --> 00:22:36,670
There's no time for a social life. Where are you gonna meet someone?
根本沒有可以社交的時間 要去哪裡認識朋友呢？

340
00:22:36,850 --> 00:22:38,440
- Well.. - Mommy, I can't..
-那個… -媽咪，我找不…

341
00:22:38,620 --> 00:22:40,780
Sea shore? Row boat.
海邊嗎？在小船上

342
00:22:44,390 --> 00:22:49,450
Let's say, I don't know, you met someone in the pediatrician's office.
我想，我不知道 可以在小兒科醫生那裡認識人吧

343
00:22:50,730 --> 00:22:53,100
Rossie? We're ready for you.
小羅斯？輪到你了

344
00:23:01,510 --> 00:23:03,000
Yeah..
是啊…

345
00:23:05,080 --> 00:23:09,110
Come on, Ross Jr. It's time to go in.
走吧，小羅斯 輪到我們了

346
00:23:10,450 --> 00:23:12,440
Mommy.
媽咪

347
00:23:16,390 --> 00:23:18,480
Mommy, what's wrong with that man?
媽咪，那個人是怎麼了？

348
00:23:18,660 --> 00:23:21,020
Hey, I helped you find Waldo!
嘿，是我幫你找到華多的耶！

349
00:23:28,600 --> 00:23:31,730
- Good, you haven't left yet. - Where have you been?
-太好了，你還沒走 -你去哪了？

350
00:23:31,910 --> 00:23:35,310
I got held up at Dr. Gettleman's office.
有事情在葛曼醫師那耽擱了一下

351
00:23:35,510 --> 00:23:40,210
There was some guy that freaked everybody out.
有一個人嚇壞了所有的人

352
00:23:40,410 --> 00:23:43,410
I don't think I'm going back there.
我想我再也不要回去那裡了

353
00:23:43,620 --> 00:23:46,310
You got here just in time. I really have to go, buddy.
你正好趕上 我得要走了，兄弟

354
00:23:46,490 --> 00:23:47,510
Oh, man.
喔，真是的

355
00:23:47,690 --> 00:23:51,520
- Promise to call me when you land? - Of course I will. I love you.
-答應我一下飛機就打電話 -當然，我愛你

356
00:23:51,690 --> 00:23:52,850
I love you too.
我也愛你

357
00:23:58,000 --> 00:24:01,900
Watch the tongue, people. We got a baby over here.
不要舌吻，你們，兒童不宜

358
00:24:02,400 --> 00:24:05,240
- Bye, Chandler. - Bye.
-再見，錢德 -再見

359
00:24:05,410 --> 00:24:07,770
- Bye, honey. - Bye.
-再見，親愛的 -再見

360
00:24:12,180 --> 00:24:16,010
- What's the matter, Joe? - I'm mad at you for leaving.
-怎麼了，喬伊？ -我很生氣你要走

361
00:24:16,180 --> 00:24:19,980
You know, you're nothing but a big leaver.
你知道嗎？你什麼都不會 就最會拋棄人家

362
00:24:20,290 --> 00:24:23,690
A big leaver with a stupid suitcase.
帶著笨行李的負心漢

363
00:24:25,590 --> 00:24:30,390
Any chance you're trying to pick a fight to make all of this easier?
你是不是故意說一些氣話 讓自己好過點呢？

364
00:24:33,170 --> 00:24:36,400
Dude, you see right through me!
老兄，你真是太瞭解我了！

365
00:24:45,310 --> 00:24:47,710
Okay, well.. Bye, Mon.
好了，那麼…再見了，摩妮卡

366
00:24:48,380 --> 00:24:50,410
Bye, Ross. Rachel.
再見，羅斯，瑞秋

367
00:24:51,020 --> 00:24:54,180
- Bye, Emma. - Okay, bye-bye.
-再見，艾□ -好了，拜拜

368
00:24:54,350 --> 00:24:57,550
Have a good trip. Okay. Oh, my God.
旅途愉快，好了，喔，天啊

369
00:25:01,700 --> 00:25:03,530
Wait.
錢德，等一下

370
00:25:04,930 --> 00:25:07,900
It goes old job..
應該是舊工作…

371
00:25:08,070 --> 00:25:10,130
new job..
新工作…

372
00:25:10,340 --> 00:25:11,530
and you.
然後是你

373
00:25:13,640 --> 00:25:15,700
This is just something I have to do.
那只不過是我要做的工作

374
00:25:16,240 --> 00:25:18,300
I know.
我知道

375
00:25:18,480 --> 00:25:20,810
I love you so much.
我好愛你

376
00:25:20,980 --> 00:25:23,610
I know that too.
我也知道

377
00:25:34,090 --> 00:25:37,930
Don't worry. I'll be back before you know it.
別擔心 我很快就會回來了

378
00:25:38,100 --> 00:25:39,860
Yes, it will be the same.
是的，一切都不會變

379
00:25:40,630 --> 00:25:43,230
Because I know, that's how.
因為我就是知道

380
00:25:43,400 --> 00:25:44,460
I promise.
我保證

381
00:25:44,640 --> 00:25:45,970
You double promise?
你可以雙重保證嗎？

382
00:25:50,610 --> 00:25:52,240
Call me when you land.
一下機就打電話給我

383
00:25:53,810 --> 00:25:56,180
- Can I talk now? - Okay, bye.
-輪到我講了嗎？ -好的，再見

384
00:25:56,380 --> 00:25:58,210
- Joey! - He had to board.
-喬伊！ -他要登機了

385
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:00,000


386
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:00,000
